Recommended implementation priority
For the best development outcome, I recommend building MsmeBooks Academy in three phases rather than attempting every advanced feature at once.

Phase 1
Launch the core Academy

Public landing page, course catalog, student and instructor dashboards, course player, assessments, payments, and verifiable certificates.

Phase 2
Expand training operations

Live classes, corporate training, partner certification, instructor analytics, course bundles, and subscriptions.

Phase 3
Introduce advanced intelligence

AI learning assistant, practical MsmeBooks software sandbox, personalized learning paths, advanced analytics, and mobile offline learning.

Strategic recommendation: Make the Academy a direct extension of the MsmeBooks SaaS platform, so a customer can subscribe to MsmeBooks, learn to use the software, train employees, and obtain certification through one connected ecosystem. This also creates opportunities for recurring training revenue, improved customer onboarding, and a stronger certified partner network.




